#: ../../source/config_package.rst:217
msgid ""
"Each dependency becomes a subpackage of the current package. All subfolders "
"of the current package are considered subpackages (of the type `local`) if "
"they contain a ``partcad.yaml`` file. Subfolders do not need to be "
"explicitly declared as a dependency, but may be declared to provide a more "
"detailed description."
msgstr ""
"Cada dependencia se convierte en un subpaquete del paquete actual. Todos los "
"subdirectorios del paquete actual se consideran subpaquetes (del tipo "
"`local`) si contienen un archivo ``partcad.yaml``. Los subdirectorios no "
"necesitan declararse explícitamente como una dependencia, pero pueden "
"declararse para proporcionar una descripción más detallada."

#: ../../source/config_package.rst:222
msgid "External packages"
msgstr "Paquetes externos"

#: ../../source/config_package.rst:224
msgid ""
"A dependency of type ``external`` is a package whose contents are served by "
"a **repository plugin** instead of being read from a folder (``local``) or a "
"remote archive (``git``, ``tar``). Its ``plugin`` field references a "
"repository declared in the ``repositories`` section (see :ref:"
"`repositories`):"
msgstr ""
"Una dependencia de tipo ``external`` es un paquete cuyo contenido es servido "
"por un **plugin de repositorio** en lugar de leerse desde una carpeta "
"(``local``) o un archivo remoto (``git``, ``tar``). Su campo ``plugin`` "
"referencia un repositorio declarado en la sección ``repositories`` "
"(consulte :ref:`repositories`):"

#: ../../source/config_package.rst:240
msgid ""
"The package's objects (parts, sketches, assemblies, ...), its child "
"packages, and its metadata are all fetched from the plugin on demand, rather "
"than being enumerated up front. This keeps loading cheap even when the "
"repository is large or remote: a part is fetched only when it is actually "
"used."
msgstr ""
"Los objetos del paquete (piezas, bocetos, ensamblajes, ...), sus paquetes "
"hijos y sus metadatos se obtienen todos del plugin bajo demanda, en lugar de "
"enumerarse por adelantado. Esto mantiene la carga económica incluso cuando "
"el repositorio es grande o remoto: una pieza se obtiene solo cuando "
"realmente se usa."

#: ../../source/config_package.rst:245
msgid ""
"An external package can host a hierarchy. When its children are listed, the "
"plugin reports child package names; each child is imported as another "
"external package backed by the same plugin, with a ``subfolder`` that scopes "
"its requests within the repository. In this way one plugin can serve an "
"entire tree of packages, each with its own sketches, parts, assemblies, "
"providers and further children."
msgstr ""
"Un paquete externo puede alojar una jerarquía. Cuando se enumeran sus hijos, "
"el plugin reporta los nombres de los paquetes hijos; cada hijo se importa "
"como otro paquete externo respaldado por el mismo plugin, con un "
"``subfolder`` que delimita el alcance de sus solicitudes dentro del "
"repositorio. De esta manera, un solo plugin puede servir un árbol completo "
"de paquetes, cada uno con sus propios bocetos, piezas, ensamblajes, "
"proveedores y más hijos."

#: ../../source/config_package.rst:252
msgid ""
"Non-null responses from a plugin are cached on disk, keyed by the plugin "
"reference and the request; a request the plugin has no answer for is "
"remembered only for the run that made it, and is put to the plugin again "
"after a restart. The same key also names the directory the plugin's own "
"files are materialized into, and a file already there is served without "
"asking the plugin again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/config_package.rst:258
msgid ""
"The cache does not know when the plugin's code changes, so a plugin that "
"starts answering differently - a new field on every part it serves, or the "
"same parts measured another way - would keep being served the stale, pre-"
"change entries. The plugin says so itself, with a module-level constant in "
"its script::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/config_package.rst:268
msgid ""
"It is folded into the cache location, so raising it moves the whole "
"repository (and every child in its hierarchy) to a fresh cache namespace at "
"once. It defaults to ``0`` when the script names none, and a repository with "
"no script of its own - an ``enrich`` one, which rewrites another "
"repository's answers - has no code to version and stays at ``0``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/config_package.rst:274
msgid ""
"The number lives in the plugin because it is the plugin's own business. A "
"package that imports a plugin-backed library has no way of knowing that the "
"library now measures its parts differently, and should not have to be told: "
"it would have to be told again in every package that imports it, and each of "
"them would be a place to forget. So this is not a field of the dependency "
"that imports the plugin, and PartCAD reads it out of the script rather than "
"asking for it - the answer is needed before the first question can be asked. "
"The script is parsed, never executed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/config_package.rst:283
msgid ""
"See ``examples/plugin_repository_basic`` (a package backed by a local file), "
"``examples/plugin_repository_full`` (backed by an HTTP endpoint) and "
"``examples/plugin_repository_tree`` (a hierarchy of packages)."
msgstr ""
"Consulte ``examples/plugin_repository_basic`` (un paquete respaldado por un "
"archivo local), ``examples/plugin_repository_full`` (respaldado por un "
"endpoint HTTP) y ``examples/plugin_repository_tree`` (una jerarquía de "
"paquetes)."

#: ../../source/config_package.rst:291
msgid "Repositories"
msgstr "Repositorios"

#: ../../source/config_package.rst:293
msgid ""
"A repository plugin serves the contents of a package: its objects, its child "
"packages and its metadata. It is what backs an ``external`` dependency (see "
"`External packages`_)."
msgstr ""
"Un plugin de repositorio sirve el contenido de un paquete: sus objetos, sus "
"paquetes hijos y sus metadatos. Es lo que respalda una dependencia "
"``external`` (consulte `External packages`_)."

#: ../../source/config_package.rst:297
msgid ""
"Repositories are declared in ``partcad.yaml`` using the following syntax:"
msgstr ""
"Los repositorios se declaran en ``partcad.yaml`` usando la siguiente "
"sintaxis:"

#: ../../source/config_package.rst:311
msgid ""
"``enrich`` repositories are references to other repositories with some "
"parameters modified to specific values."
msgstr ""
"Los repositorios ``enrich`` son referencias a otros repositorios con algunos "
"parámetros modificados a valores específicos."

#: ../../source/config_package.rst:314
msgid ""
"``basic`` repositories are implemented as Python scripts, invoked the same "
"way as provider scripts (via ``runpy``, with the input in the global "
"``request`` and the output in the global ``output``). A repository script "
"answers a single, generic key/value request:"
msgstr ""
"Los repositorios ``basic`` se implementan como scripts de Python, invocados "
"de la misma manera que los scripts de proveedores (mediante ``runpy``, con "
"la entrada en el global ``request`` y la salida en el global ``output``). Un "
"script de repositorio responde a una única solicitud genérica de clave/valor:"

#: ../../source/config_package.rst:319
msgid "`request[\"api\"] == \"get\"`"
msgstr "`request[\"api\"] == \"get\"`"

#: ../../source/config_package.rst:320
msgid "`request[\"key\"]`: the key being requested"
msgstr "`request[\"key\"]`: la clave que se solicita"

#: ../../source/config_package.rst:321
msgid ""
"`output[\"result\"]`: the value stored under that key (or ``null`` if "
"unknown)"
msgstr ""
"`output[\"result\"]`: el valor almacenado bajo esa clave (o ``null`` si se "
"desconoce)"

#: ../../source/config_package.rst:323
msgid ""
"The keys address every kind of data uniformly, so serving a new kind of "
"object or a new piece of metadata needs no new API:"
msgstr ""
"Las claves direccionan todo tipo de datos de manera uniforme, por lo que "
"servir un nuevo tipo de objeto o un nuevo dato de metadatos no requiere una "
"nueva API:"

#: ../../source/config_package.rst:326
msgid ""
"``objects/<kind>`` -- all objects of a kind, as ``{name: config, ...}``. The "
"kinds are the ten in ``Project.OBJECT_KINDS``: ``material``, ``interface``, "
"``sketch``, ``part``, ``assembly``, ``scene``, ``provider``, ``repository``, "
"``software``, ``partType``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/config_package.rst:330
msgid ""
"``objects/<kind>/<name>`` -- a single object's config, fetched without "
"listing the whole repository"
msgstr ""
"``objects/<kind>/<name>`` -- la configuración de un único objeto, obtenida "
"sin listar todo el repositorio"

#: ../../source/config_package.rst:332
msgid "``deps`` -- the names of the child packages"
msgstr "``deps`` -- los nombres de los paquetes hijos"

#: ../../source/config_package.rst:333
msgid ""
"``meta`` -- package-level properties (``desc``, ``render``, "
"``manufacturable``, ``suppliers``, ...), and ``objectKinds`` (see below)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/config_package.rst:335
msgid ""
"``files/<path>`` -- the base64-encoded content of a file an object "
"references by ``path``. A plugin-backed package has no source tree, so a "
"file-backed object's file is fetched from the plugin and materialized into "
"the package's cache directory when the object is built."
msgstr ""
"``files/<path>`` -- el contenido codificado en base64 de un archivo que un "
"objeto referencia mediante ``path``. Un paquete respaldado por un plugin no "
"tiene árbol fuente, por lo que el archivo de un objeto basado en archivo se "
"obtiene del plugin y se materializa en el directorio de caché del paquete "
"cuando se construye el objeto."

#: ../../source/config_package.rst:340
msgid ""
"For a hierarchy, a child package's requests are prefixed with its "
"``subfolder``: a child in ``motors`` asks for ``motors/objects/part``, "
"``motors/deps`` and so on, all served by the same script."
msgstr ""
"Para una jerarquía, las solicitudes de un paquete hijo se prefijan con su "
"``subfolder``: un hijo en ``motors`` solicita ``motors/objects/part``, "
"``motors/deps``, etc., todos servidos por el mismo script."

#: ../../source/config_package.rst:345
msgid "Say which kinds a package has"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/config_package.rst:347
msgid ""
"Every key is a separate run of the script, and a package has ten kinds of "
"object. Something as ordinary as listing the packages that hold anything to "
"look at asks after four of them, per package, and for a hierarchy of a "
"hundred packages that is four hundred runs -- most of them to be told "
"\"none\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/config_package.rst:352
msgid ""
"A package's ``meta`` may therefore carry ``objectKinds``, the kinds that "
"package holds at all:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/config_package.rst:359
msgid ""
"PartCAD then answers \"none\" for every other kind without asking. This "
"narrows what is asked for and never what may be served: a plugin that lists "
"a kind it turns out to have none of is simply asked a question it answers "
"emptily, and a plugin that says nothing is asked about everything, as "
"before. It is read out of the metadata PartCAD has already fetched and is "
"never worth a request of its own, so a package reached on its own -- rather "
"than through a traversal, which reads ``meta`` for every package as it goes "
"-- is queried exactly as it was."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/config_package.rst:367
msgid ""
"Responses are cached per key (in memory and on disk), so a repository that "
"is slow or remote is queried as little as possible. See ``examples/"
"plugin_repository_basic``, ``examples/plugin_repository_full`` (an HTTP-"
"backed repository) and ``examples/plugin_repository_tree`` (a hierarchy)."
msgstr ""
"Las respuestas se almacenan en caché por clave (en memoria y en disco), de "
"modo que un repositorio lento o remoto se consulte lo menos posible. "
"Consulte ``examples/plugin_repository_basic``, ``examples/"
"plugin_repository_full`` (un repositorio respaldado por HTTP) y ``examples/"
"plugin_repository_tree`` (una jerarquía)."
